      a: "LAG(revenue) OVER (ORDER BY month) pairs each month with its predecessor — 2024-02 reads 3731.97 against its own 3609.64, and the momentum is the difference. The first month has no predecessor, so LAG returns NULL, and the report should say 'baseline month' rather than coalescing a fake zero into a delta column. The trap is the filtered spine: a WHERE or HAVING that drops a month shrinks the window's input, and the next surviving month reads its predecessor from whatever survived — filter out 2024-06 and July's LAG reaches back to May's 2910.31, reporting a two-month gap as one month's move. That is not a bug in LAG; it is the definition of 'previous row in the window' being narrower than 'previous calendar month'. The habit: build the month spine unfiltered in a CTE, run LAG there, and apply business gates AFTER the momentum is computed — or state loudly that the filtered version measures a different thing.",
